ource":["The `bus_sizes` argument of `n.plot()` can be even more powerful. It can produce pie charts, e.g. for the mix of electricity generation at each bus.\n","\n","The dispatch of each generator, we can find at:"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":59,"metadata":{"id":"aOC-s-yQTKHZ","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791452932786,"user_tz":-120,"elapsed":10,"user":{"displayName":"Ariz Salac","userId":"14132994972447731579"}},"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"outputId":"f8cbccc7-3bdd-40ee-90f9-76efebd90f0c"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["name\n","07TPLPB4_U01          0.000000\n","07TPLPB4_U02          0.000000\n","07TPLPB4_U03          0.000000\n","07TPLPB4_U04          0.000000\n","07BDPP_U01            0.000000\n","07BDPP_U02            0.000000\n","07BDPP_U03            0.000000\n","07BDPP_U04            0.000000\n","07JANOPO_G01         60.000000\n","07LOBOC_G01          14.400000\n","07LOBOC_G02          14.400000\n","07SEVILL_G01         30.000000\n","Grid_electricity    639.032139\n","dtype: float64"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":59}],"source":["n.generators_t.p.sum()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"1SedkY2kTKHZ"},"source":["If we group this by the **bus** and **carrier**..."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":60,"metadata":{"id":"65ryrEKPTKHZ","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791452935860,"user_tz":-120,"elapsed":6,"user":{"displayName":"Ariz Salac","userId":"14132994972447731579"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["s = n.generators_t.p.sum().groupby([n.generators.bus, n.generators.carrier]).sum()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"gBcUl4o1TKHa"},"source":["... we get a multi-indexed `pandas.Series` ..."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":61,"metadata":{"id":"mm8c3zOZTKHa","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791452938800,"user_tz":-120,"elapsed":22,"user":{"displayName":"Ariz Salac","userId":"14132994972447731579"}},"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"outputId":"7bd23858-c732-4c32-bc1c-42c94bed9656"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["bus        carrier\n","07CORELLA  Diesel       0.000000\n","           Hydro      118.800000\n","07TAPAL    Diesel       0.000000\n","07UBAY     Grid       639.032139\n","dtype: float64"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":61}],"source":["s"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"dSdcpbczTKHa"},"source":["... which we can pass to `n.plot(bus_sizes=...)`:"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":62,"metadata":{"id":"Jbbmk7TyTKHa","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791452940296,"user_tz":-120,"elapsed":163,"user":{"displayName":"Ariz Salac","userId":"14132994972447731579"}},"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":356},"outputId":"590584eb-c1bd-4ebc-e07b-cbf4459abd8f"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["n.plot(margin=1, bus_sizes=s / 3000);"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"v4UPehXBTKHa"},"source":["**How does this magic work?** The plotting function will look up the colors specified in `n.carriers` for each carrier and match it with the second index-level of `s`."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Now, we make complex plotting functions to aid our analyis:"],"metadata":{"id":"xA1dTnsuKeyx"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# prompt: generate me the percentages on the generation mix of different carriers. plot as a pie chart with values outside. make it a function and use the colors in the n.carriers\n","\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","def plot_generation_mix_pie(n):\n","  \"\"\"\n","  Plots the generation mix of different carriers as a pie chart with percentages outside.\n","\n","  Args:\n","    network (pypsa.Network): The PyPSA network object.\n","  \"\"\"\n","  # Calculate total generation per carrier\n","  generation_by_carrier = n.generators_t.p.sum().groupby(n.generators.carrier).sum()\n","\n","  # Calculate percentages\n","  total_generation = generation_by_carrier.sum()\n","  percentages = generation_by_carrier / total_generation * 100\n","\n","  # Get carrier colors\n","  carrier_colors = n.carriers.color.dropna().to_dict()\n","\n","  # Filter out carriers with zero generation\n","  percentages = percentages[percentages > 0]\n","  labels = percentages.index\n","  sizes = percentages.values\n","  colors = [carrier_colors.get(label, 'gray') for label in labels] # Use gray for carriers without a specified color\n","\n","  fig1, ax1 = plt.subplots()\n","  patches, texts, autotexts = ax1.pie(sizes, labels=labels, colors=colors, autopct='%1.1f%%',\n","                                      startangle=90, pctdistance=1.1, labeldistance=1.2)\n","\n","  # Ensure text is visible\n","  for text in texts:\n","      text.set_color('black')\n","  for autotext in autotexts:\n","      autotext.set_color('black')\n","\n","  ax1.axis('equal')  # Equal aspect ratio ensures that pie is drawn as a circle.\n","  plt.title(\"Generation Mix by Carrier\")\n","  plt.show()\n","\n","# Call the function with your network object\n","plot_generation_mix_pie(n)"],"metadata":{"id":"RKn8ypW9Kdda","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791453138297,"user_tz":-120,"elapsed":68,"user":{"displayName":"Ariz Salac","userId":"14132994972447731579"}},"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":428},"outputId":"36bf0259-ead6-482c-a92a-294de84747bc"},"execution_count":64,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# prompt: make me a function that makes a stacked plot for the different generator and storage unit (discharging and charging) carriers. Use the colors in the n.carriers. Also, add a line plot for the total load.\n","\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import pandas as pd\n","\n","def plot_generation_and_load(n):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Makes a stacked plot for the different generator and storage unit (discharging) carriers.\n","    Uses the colors in the n.carriers. Also, adds a line plot for the total load.\n","\n","    Args:\n","        n (pypsa.Network): The optimized PyPSA network.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    # Transpose and group generators by carrier along the columns, then transpose back\n","    generation_by_carrier = n.generators_t.p.T.groupby(n.generators.carrier).sum().T\n","\n","    # Group storage units by carrier (discharging is positive)\n","    if not n.storage_units.empty:\n","        storage_discharging_by_carrier = n.storage_units_t.p.T.groupby(n.storage_units.carrier).sum().T\n","        storage_discharging_by_carrier = storage_discharging_by_carrier.clip(lower=0)\n","        # Combine generators and storage discharging\n","        combined_output = pd.concat([generation_by_carrier, storage_discharging_by_carrier], axis=1).T.groupby(level=0).sum().T\n","    else:\n","        combined_output = generation_by_carrier\n","\n","    # Get total load\n","    total_load = n.loads_t.p_set.sum(axis=1)\n","\n","    # Get colors from carriers\n","    carrier_colors = n.carriers.color.dropna().to_dict()\n","\n","    # Plotting\n","    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6))\n","\n","    # Stacked plot of generation and storage discharging by carrier\n","    combined_output.plot(kind='area', stacked=True, ax=ax, color=[carrier_colors.get(c, 'gray') for c in combined_output.columns])\n","\n","    # Plot total load as a line\n","    total_load.plot(ax=ax, color='black', linestyle='--', linewidth=2, label='Total Load')\n","\n","    ax.set_xlabel(\"Time\")\n","    ax.set_ylabel(\"Power (MW)\")\n","    ax.set_title(\"Generation and Storage Discharging by Carrier vs Total Load\")\n","    ax.legend(title=\"Carrier\")\n","    plt.grid(True)\n","    plt.tight_layout()\n","    plt.show()\n","\n","# Call the function with your network\n","plot_generation_and_load(n)"],"metadata":{"id":"32FpsvYiKaf0","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791453181619,"user_tz":-120,"elapsed":363,"user":{"displayName":"Ariz Salac","userId":"14132994972447731579"}},"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":488},"outputId":"a2c59fb3-8426-4b73-9bf4-a3e51473d699"},"execution_count":65,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# prompt: make me a function that gives me a map plot showing the buses (with pie chart of generation capacities) and transmission lines (with loading as color, and direction of flow) at specific time input for a network.\n","\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import cartopy.crs as ccrs\n","import numpy as np\n","\n","def plot_network_at_time(n, time_snapshot):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Plots the PyPSA network at a specific time snapshot.\n","    Shows buses with pie charts of generation capacities, and transmission lines\n","    with loading as color and direction of flow.\n","\n","    Args:\n","        n (pypsa.Network): The optimized PyPSA network.\n","        time_snapshot (pandas.Timestamp or str): The time snapshot to plot.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    # Ensure the time_snapshot is a pandas Timestamp\n","    if isinstance(time_snapshot, str):\n","        time_snapshot = pd.to_datetime(time_snapshot)\n","\n","    # Check if the snapshot exists in the network\n","    if time_snapshot not in n.snapshots:\n","        print(f\"Error: Time snapshot '{time_snapshot}' not found in the network.\")\n","        print(\"Available snapshots:\", n.snapshots)\n","        return\n","\n","    fig = plt.figure(figsize=(15, 15))\n","    ax = fig.add_subplot(1, 1, 1, projection=ccrs.PlateCarree())\n","    ax.set_extent([124.0, 124.5, 9.5, 10.5], crs=ccrs.PlateCarree()) # Adjust extent for Bohol\n","\n","    # Plot buses\n","    for bus in n.buses.itertuples():\n","        ax.plot(bus.x, bus.y, 'o', color='black', markersize=5, transform=ccrs.PlateCarree())\n","        ax.text(bus.x + 0.01, bus.y + 0.01, bus.index, fontsize=8, transform=ccrs.PlateCarree())\n","\n","        # Create pie chart for generation at this bus\n","        bus_generators = n.generators[n.generators.bus == bus.Index]\n","        if not bus_generators.empty:\n","            generation_at_bus = n.generators_t.p.loc[time_snapshot, bus_generators.index].sum()\n","            if generation_at_bus > 0:\n","                generation_shares = n.generators_t.p.loc[time_snapshot, bus_generators.index]\n","                generation_shares = generation_shares[generation_shares > 0] # Only include generators with output\n","\n","                if not generation_shares.empty:\n","                     # Get colors from carriers\n","                    carrier_colors = n.carriers.color.to_dict()\n","                    colors = [carrier_colors.get(n.generators.loc[gen_name].carrier, 'gray') for gen_name in generation_shares.index]\n","\n","                    # Scale pie chart size based on total generation at the bus\n","                    total_generation = generation_shares.sum()\n","                    pie_radius = 0.05 + total_generation / (500) * 0.05  # Adjust scaling factor as needed\n","\n","                    # Create the pie chart as an annotation\n","                    ax.pie(generation_shares, colors=colors, radius=pie_radius, center=(bus.x, bus.y), frame=True,\n","                           wedgeprops={\"edgecolor\":\"white\",'linewidth': 0.5, 'antialiased': True})\n","\n","\n","    # Plot lines with loading and direction\n","    # Calculate line loading percentage and direction\n","    line_loading = n.lines_t.p0.loc[time_snapshot] / n.lines.s_nom * 100\n","    line_direction = np.sign(n.lines_t.p0.loc[time_snapshot]) # Positive for flow from bus0 to bus1\n","\n","    for line in n.lines.itertuples():\n","        bus0_coords = (n.buses.loc[line.bus0].x, n.buses.loc[line.bus0].y)\n","        bus1_coords = (n.buses.loc[line.bus1].x, n.buses.loc[line.bus1].y)\n","\n","        loading_pct = abs(line_loading.get(line.Index, 0)) # Get loading, default to 0 if not found\n","        flow_direction = line_direction.get(line.Index, 0)\n","\n","        # Determine color based on loading\n","        if loading_pct < 20:\n","            color = 'green'\n","        elif loading_pct < 60:\n","            color = 'orange'\n","        else:\n","            color = 'red'\n","\n","        # Determine line style and thickness based on loading\n","        linewidth = 1 + loading_pct / 50 # Increase thickness with loading\n","        linestyle = '-'\n","\n","        # Plot the line\n","        ax.plot([bus0_coords[0], bus1_coords[0]], [bus0_coords[1], bus1_coords[1]],\n","                color=color, linewidth=linewidth, linestyle=linestyle, transform=ccrs.PlateCarree())\n","\n","        # Add arrows to indicate flow direction\n","        if flow_direction != 0:\n","            mid_point_x = (bus0_coords[0] + bus1_coords[0]) / 2\n","            mid_point_y = (bus0_coords[1] + bus1_coords[1]) / 2\n","\n","            if flow_direction > 0: # Flow from bus0 to bus1\n","                dx = bus1_coords[0] - bus0_coords[0]\n","                dy = bus1_coords[1] - bus0_coords[1]\n","            else: # Flow from bus1 to bus0\n","                dx = bus0_coords[0] - bus1_coords[0]\n","                dy = bus0_coords[1] - bus1_coords[1]\n","\n","            # Add arrow annotation\n","            ax.arrow(mid_point_x, mid_point_y, dx * 0.1, dy * 0.1,\n","                     head_width=0.015, head_length=0.02, fc='black', ec='black',\n","                     transform=ccrs.PlateCarree())\n","\n","\n","    ax.set_title(f'Network Plot at {time_snapshot.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\")}')\n","    ax.coastlines()\n","    ax.gridlines(draw_labels=True, linewidth=2, color='gray', alpha=0.5, linestyle='--')\n","    plt.show()\n","\n","# Example usage:\n","# Choose a time snapshot from you